//@version=6
// =============================================================================
//  EDGELOG - POINT SCORE 1.0 -- the owner's 9-point score on the signal bar
//  Pine port of docs/POINT_SCORE_SPEC.md (spec v1.2, "ps1.2") and of tools/point_score.py
//  v1.2 (2026-10-02): the four "200" lines are a plain moving average (SMA) by default; the
//  "Moving average" setting switches them to the EMA of v1.1.
//
//  WHAT IT IS
//  At the CLOSE of every bar it scores the nine points from the spec, for the LONG
//  side and for the SHORT side at the same time, then shows the score of the last
//  closed bar in a table, labels strong bars, and can fire an alert.
//  The bar that has just closed IS the signal bar S of the spec (the last closed bar
//  before an entry fill). Nothing that starts at or after the bar's close is read.
//
//  MEANT FOR A 1-MINUTE CHART (the spec only supports 1m in v1). On any other chart
//  timeframe the table shows a warning, and the numbers are NOT the spec's numbers.
//  Use the normal 24-hour futures session (extended hours ON) - the spec's 1m / 5m /
//  30m EMAs run over 24-hour bars.
//
//  THE NINE POINTS (long; short mirrors each one with < in place of >)
//   1-4  close above the 200 moving average (SMA default, EMA setting) of the 10-second /
//        1-minute / 5-minute / 30-minute bars
//        - 1m  : the average of this chart's closes, includes the signal bar.
//        - 10s : last 10-second bar inside the signal bar (request.security_lower_tf).
//        - 5m / 30m : the HTF bar BEFORE the one holding the signal bar (non-repainting).
//        - each average is NA until its own timeframe has a full 200-bar window (SMA) or 600
//          bars (EMA).
//   5-7  close above yesterday's regular-session low / close / high. Yesterday = the most
//        recent earlier New York date that has regular-session bars (09:30 to 16:00) and is
//        NOT a listed CME holiday (HOL_FULL below: a holiday's Globex stub is never a regular
//        session). Yesterday must also be COMPLETE: its last regular bar is 15:59 (13:14 on a
//        listed early-close day, HOL_EARLY), else its three levels and the trend are NA.
//        Sessions are tracked from the 1m bars themselves, NOT with a daily request
//        (TradingView's daily futures bar is the overnight session).
//   8    largest body since today's low (long: green candle, body >= every body from the
//        latest bar whose low <= all earlier lows today, through this bar).
//        Short: red candle, window starts at the latest bar whose high >= all earlier highs.
//   9    largest volume since today's low (short: high). No colour test.
//   Trend (separate, never in the /9): yesterday's high AND low both above (short: both below)
//        the day before's.
//  total = hits among the 9. max = points that are not NA. NA is never a miss: "7/8".
//
//  PARITY EXPORT
//  The data-window plots named "L ..." / "S ..." / "R ..." are for Export chart data
//  (chart menu -> Export chart data). 1 = hit, 0 = miss, empty = NA. They do not draw on
//  the chart. python tools/point_score.py parity <csv> --root NQ compares them with EDGE LOG.
//
//  KNOWN LIMITS
//   - Turn ON TradingView's back-adjustment for continuous futures (the B-ADJ button at the
//     bottom of the chart, "Adjust for contracts changes" in the chart settings). Without it the
//     30-minute EMA carries the roll gap for about two weeks after every quarterly roll, and the
//     first session after a roll reads yesterday's levels from the old contract.
//   - The CME holiday list (HOL_FULL / HOL_EARLY below) must be EXTENDED EACH DECEMBER from the
//     CME holiday calendar; it must match CME_HOLIDAYS in tools/point_score.py. A day missing
//     from the list cannot give a wrong level: its stub fails the completeness test and reads NA.
//   - The 30-minute average needs 200 30-minute bars for the SMA (about 4-5 trading days) or about
//     600 for the EMA (about 13 trading days). A 1-minute chart on the Premium plan loads 20,000
//     bars, which only just reaches the EMA's 600. The
//     table's bottom row shows how many bars each timeframe has; "warming up" = NA points.
//   - 10-second bars need a TradingView plan with seconds timeframes (Premium or higher).
//     TradingView may also only load 100,000 intrabars, so the oldest part of a long chart
//     can have no 10-second data. Those bars show NA for the 10s point (never a miss).
//     If the script will not run on your plan, untick "Use 10-second data".
//   - Volume can differ slightly between feeds (ties on the volume point can flip).
//   - Yesterday's levels and the 1m EMA start from the first bar the chart has loaded; a
//     session (or today's window) that was cut off by the start of the loaded history is
//     ignored (NA), and the 1m EMA is seeded from the first loaded close (as in the spec).
//   - At the live bar's close the last 10-second bar may arrive a moment late.
// =============================================================================
indicator("EDGELOG Point Score 1.0", shorttitle = "POINTS", overlay = true, max_labels_count = 500)

// -- Inputs --------------------------------------------------------------------
G_PT = "Point score"
G_TF = "Timeframes"
G_MK = "Market and sessions"
G_SH = "Display and alerts"

sideIn    = input.string("Auto", "Side", options = ["Auto", "Long", "Short"], group = G_PT, tooltip = "Auto = long when the bar closes up (close >= open), short otherwise. Long / Short force one side for the labels and alerts. The table and the exported columns always carry BOTH sides.")
maType    = input.string("SMA", "Moving average", options = ["SMA", "EMA"], group = G_PT, tooltip = "Spec v1.2: SMA (a plain moving average) is the default; EMA is the v1.1 line. EDGE LOG records which one a score used.")
emaLen    = input.int(200, "Moving average length", minval = 2, group = G_PT, tooltip = "The spec uses 200.")

tf10      = input.timeframe("10S", "10-second timeframe", group = G_TF)
use10     = input.bool(true, "Use 10-second data", group = G_TF, tooltip = "Needs a TradingView plan with seconds timeframes (Premium or higher). Untick it if the script errors on your plan: the 10s point then shows NA.")
tf5       = input.timeframe("5", "5-minute timeframe", group = G_TF)
tf30      = input.timeframe("30", "30-minute timeframe", group = G_TF)

mktIn     = input.string("Futures - today from 09:30", "Market", options = ["Futures - today from 09:30", "Stocks - today from 04:00"], group = G_MK, tooltip = "Where 'today' starts for points 8 and 9: 09:30 New York for futures, 04:00 for stocks.")
regSess   = input.string("0930-1600", "Regular session (New York time)", group = G_MK, tooltip = "Format hhmm-hhmm. Yesterday's high / low / close are taken from bars that START inside this window (end not included).")

showTrend = input.bool(true, "Show trend point in the table", group = G_SH, tooltip = "The trend point is shown on its own row and is never added to the /9.")
labThr    = input.int(7, "Label threshold (points)", minval = 1, maxval = 9, group = G_SH)
altThr    = input.int(8, "Alert threshold (points)", minval = 1, maxval = 9, group = G_SH)
showLbl   = input.bool(true, "Show labels", group = G_SH)
layout    = input.string("Compact", "Display", options = ["Compact", "Minimal", "Full"], group = G_SH, tooltip = "Compact: two rows of coloured cells (MA 10s 1m 5m 30m / Y-L Y-C Y-H Body Vol), the side and score, and the trend. Minimal: one score badge - Hit colour at or above the label threshold, Miss colour below half the points, NA colour in between - plus the trend. Full: the detailed table.")
tblPos    = input.string("Top right", "Table position", options = ["Top left", "Top center", "Top right", "Middle left", "Middle center", "Middle right", "Bottom left", "Bottom center", "Bottom right"], group = G_SH)

// -- Constants -----------------------------------------------------------------
const string TZ      = "America/New_York"
const int    MIN_BARS = 600        // spec: an EMA needs 600 bars of its own timeframe (an SMA: a full window)
const int    GAP_MAX  = 7          // spec: the prior session must lie within 7 calendar days
const int    DAY_MS   = 86400000
const int    EARLY_LAST_MIN = 13 * 60 + 14   // spec: a listed early-close session ends with its 13:14 bar

// CME equity-index holidays, spec section 7 (the SAME list as CME_HOLIDAYS in tools/point_score.py). yyyymmdd keys of
// the New York date. EXTEND BOTH ARRAYS EACH DECEMBER from the CME holiday calendar.
//   HOL_FULL : no regular session. Globex may print a short stub; those bars are NOT regular-session bars, so a
//              holiday never becomes "yesterday".
//   HOL_EARLY: a regular session that ends with its 13:14 bar (complete at 13:14 instead of 15:59).
var array<int> HOL_FULL  = array.from(20250101, 20250109, 20250120, 20250217, 20250418, 20250526, 20250619, 20250704, 20250901, 20251127, 20251225, 20260101, 20260119, 20260216, 20260403, 20260525, 20260619, 20260703, 20260907, 20261126, 20261225, 20270101, 20270118, 20270215, 20270326, 20270531, 20270618, 20270705, 20270906, 20271125, 20271224)
var array<int> HOL_EARLY = array.from(20250703, 20251128, 20251224, 20261127, 20261224, 20271126)

// Table colours: mono, no hue.
color C_BG    = #1b1f27
color C_BORD  = #363a45
color C_HDR   = #262b34
color C_AUTO  = #2e343e
color C_TXT   = #e6e6e6
color C_DIM   = #8a8f98
// Tick colours (owner 2026-10-02): a hit is a green tick, a miss a red cross, NA grey. EDGE LOG's mono
// theme does not apply on TradingView. Change them in Settings.
C_HIT  = input.color(color.green, "Hit color", group = G_SH, tooltip = "Colour of a hit (tick) in the table.")
C_MISS = input.color(color.red, "Miss color", group = G_SH, tooltip = "Colour of a miss (cross) in the table.")
C_NA   = input.color(color.gray, "NA color", group = G_SH, tooltip = "Colour of a point that could not be scored.")
color C_WHITE = #ffffff

int minBars = maType == "SMA" ? emaLen : MIN_BARS
int winStartMin = mktIn == "Stocks - today from 04:00" ? 240 : 570
// Minute of the day at which the regular session ends (the last 4 digits of "hhmm-hhmm").
int sessEndMin  = int(str.tonumber(str.substring(regSess, 5, 7))) * 60 + int(str.tonumber(str.substring(regSess, 7, 9)))

// -- Helper functions ----------------------------------------------------------
// Tri-state point as a float: 1.0 = hit, 0.0 = miss, na = not available.
// (Pine v6 bools cannot be na, so every point is a float.)
f_ab(float c, float lvl, bool isLong) =>
    float r = na
    if not na(c) and not na(lvl)
        r := isLong ? (c > lvl ? 1.0 : 0.0) : (c < lvl ? 1.0 : 0.0)
    r

f_cnt(float x) => na(x) ? 0.0 : 1.0

// The point's moving average of close (spec v1.2): SMA by default, EMA by setting. Both are computed on
// every bar (ta.* functions must run on every bar) and one is picked.
f_ma() =>
    float s = ta.sma(close, emaLen)
    float e = ta.ema(close, emaLen)
    maType == "SMA" ? s : e

// The average of the requested context, NA until that context has minBars bars (SMA: a full window;
// EMA: 600). Evaluated INSIDE request.security / request.security_lower_tf, so bar_index is the
// index of the foreign bar, and the average runs on the foreign series from its first bar.
f_ltf() =>
    float m = f_ma()
    bar_index >= minBars - 1 ? m : na

// Same, but one HTF bar back (used with lookahead_on so it never repaints), plus the number
// of HTF bars up to and including that reference bar.
f_htf() =>
    float m = f_ma()
    float g = bar_index >= minBars - 1 ? m : na
    [g[1], float(bar_index)]

// Table text helpers.
f_px(float x) => na(x) ? "-" : str.tostring(x, format.mintick)
f_int(float x) => na(x) ? "-" : str.tostring(int(x))
f_mark(float h) => na(h) ? "NA" : (h > 0.5 ? "✓" : "✗")
// Table position (owner 2026-10-02): any of the nine spots on the chart.
f_pos(string p) =>
    switch p
        "Top left"      => position.top_left
        "Top center"    => position.top_center
        "Top right"     => position.top_right
        "Middle left"   => position.middle_left
        "Middle center" => position.middle_center
        "Middle right"  => position.middle_right
        "Bottom left"   => position.bottom_left
        "Bottom center" => position.bottom_center
        "Bottom right"  => position.bottom_right
        => position.top_right

f_col(float h) => na(h) ? C_NA : (h > 0.5 ? C_HIT : C_MISS)
f_score(float tot, float mx) => str.tostring(int(tot)) + "/" + str.tostring(int(mx)) + (mx < 9 ? " (" + str.tostring(int(9 - mx)) + " NA)" : "")
f_warm(string nm, float n) => nm + " " + (na(n) ? "n/a" : str.tostring(int(n))) + (not na(n) and n < minBars ? " (warming up)" : "")

var array<string> KEYS = array.from("ma200_10s", "ma200_1m", "ma200_5m", "ma200_30m", "y_low", "y_close", "y_high", "big_body", "big_vol")
var array<string> LBL  = array.from("Above/Below " + str.tostring(emaLen) + " " + maType + " (10s)", "Above/Below " + str.tostring(emaLen) + " " + maType + " (1m)", "Above/Below " + str.tostring(emaLen) + " " + maType + " (5m)", "Above/Below " + str.tostring(emaLen) + " " + maType + " (30m)", "Above/Below yesterday's low", "Above/Below yesterday's close", "Above/Below yesterday's high", "Largest body since today's low/high", "Largest volume since today's low/high")

// The keys of the hit points, as a JSON list body: "ma200_1m","y_low",...
f_hits(array<float> hv) =>
    string s = ""
    for i = 0 to 8
        if array.get(hv, i) > 0.5
            s += (s == "" ? "" : ",") + '"' + array.get(KEYS, i) + '"'
    s

// -- Bar clock (all New York time; bars are stamped at their START) ------------
int  nyYear   = year(time, TZ)
int  nyMonth  = month(time, TZ)
int  nyDay    = dayofmonth(time, TZ)
int  minOfDay = hour(time, TZ) * 60 + minute(time, TZ)
int  dayTs    = timestamp(TZ, nyYear, nyMonth, nyDay, 12, 0, 0)   // noon of the NY date = the date's id
int  dayKey   = nyYear * 10000 + nyMonth * 100 + nyDay            // yyyymmdd, the key of the holiday arrays
bool isHolDay   = array.includes(HOL_FULL, dayKey)                // a listed full holiday: no regular session
bool isEarlyDay = array.includes(HOL_EARLY, dayKey)               // a listed early close: complete at 13:14
// Regular-session bar: bar START in [09:30, 16:00) on a day that is NOT a listed holiday. time() tests the start
// side; the explicit minute test guarantees the end is NOT included whatever time() does at the edge.
bool inRegSess = not na(time(timeframe.period, regSess, TZ))      // its own line: v6 evaluates and / or lazily
bool inRTH    = not isHolDay and inRegSess and minOfDay < sessEndMin
// A closing bar: the 15:59 bar (end of the regular session minus one minute), or the 13:14 bar on a listed early close.
bool isCloseBar = minOfDay == sessEndMin - 1 or (isEarlyDay and minOfDay == EARLY_LAST_MIN)

// -- Points 1-4: the four moving averages -------------------------------------
float emaRaw = f_ma()
float ema1m  = bar_index >= minBars - 1 ? emaRaw : na

// 10s: last element of the 10-second EMA array for this 1-minute bar (an empty array, e.g. no
// trades in the minute or no 10s history that far back, gives NA). request.* calls may sit in a
// conditional in v6 (dynamic requests are on by default). The timeframe test keeps the call from
// running on a chart that is not above the 10s timeframe. Pine has no try/catch, so if a plan
// without seconds timeframes makes the request itself fail, that cannot be caught from inside the
// script - that is what the "Use 10-second data" switch above is for (off = the 10s point is NA).
array<float> arr10 = array.new_float(0)
if use10 and timeframe.in_seconds() > timeframe.in_seconds(tf10)
    arr10 := request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, tf10, f_ltf())
int n10b = array.size(arr10)
float ema10 = n10b > 0 ? array.get(arr10, n10b - 1) : na
var float n10tot = 0.0
n10tot := n10tot + n10b

// 5m / 30m: the bar before the one holding the signal bar, never repainting.
[ema5, n5]   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf5,  f_htf(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[ema30, n30] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf30, f_htf(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
float n1 = bar_index + 1

// -- Points 5-7: yesterday's regular-session low / close / high ----------------
// s0 = the most recent regular session seen, s1 = the one before, s2 = the one before that.
// "ok"   = the session was seen from its first bar (not cut off by the start of the chart).
// "done" = the session's LAST regular bar so far is a closing bar (15:59, or 13:14 on a listed early close). Every
//          regular bar overwrites it, so once a session is shifted into history it says whether that session ran
//          to its close. An incomplete session (a capture hole, an unlisted short day) is NOT skipped: its levels
//          and the trend read NA instead of a wrong level (spec v1.1).
var int   s0t = na
var float s0h = na
var float s0l = na
var float s0c = na
var bool  s0ok = false
var bool  s0done = false
var int   s1t = na
var float s1h = na
var float s1l = na
var float s1c = na
var bool  s1ok = false
var bool  s1done = false
var int   s2t = na
var float s2h = na
var float s2l = na
var bool  s2ok = false
var bool  s2done = false

if inRTH
    if na(s0t) or dayTs != s0t
        // a new regular session begins: shift the history down
        s2t    := s1t
        s2h    := s1h
        s2l    := s1l
        s2ok   := s1ok
        s2done := s1done
        s1t    := s0t
        s1h    := s0h
        s1l    := s0l
        s1c    := s0c
        s1ok   := s0ok
        s1done := s0done
        s0t    := dayTs
        s0h    := high
        s0l    := low
        s0c    := close
        s0ok   := bar_index > 0
        s0done := isCloseBar
    else
        s0h    := math.max(s0h, high)
        s0l    := math.min(s0l, low)
        s0c    := close
        s0done := isCloseBar

// Yesterday = the latest session on an EARLIER date than this bar's date. Before today's
// regular session starts that is s0; once today's session has started it is s1.
bool  tdIn0 = not na(s0t) and s0t == dayTs
int   yT    = tdIn0 ? s1t : s0t
float yH    = tdIn0 ? s1h : s0h
float yL    = tdIn0 ? s1l : s0l
float yC    = tdIn0 ? s1c : s0c
bool  yOk   = tdIn0 ? (s1ok and s1done) : (s0ok and s0done)      // seen from its first bar AND ran to its close
float yyH   = tdIn0 ? s2h : s1h
float yyL   = tdIn0 ? s2l : s1l
bool  yyOk  = tdIn0 ? (s2ok and s2done) : (s1ok and s1done)
int   yyT   = tdIn0 ? s2t : s1t
int   gapD  = na(yT) ? 9999 : math.round((dayTs - yT) / DAY_MS)
int   gapYY = (na(yT) or na(yyT)) ? 9999 : math.round((yT - yyT) / DAY_MS)     // spec port: yy within 7 days of y
bool  yValid = not na(yT) and yOk and gapD <= GAP_MAX
float refYL = yValid ? yL : na
float refYC = yValid ? yC : na
float refYH = yValid ? yH : na

// -- Points 8-9: largest body / volume since today's low (long) or high (short) -
// Today window: this New York date, bar start >= 09:30 (futures) or 04:00 (stocks), no end.
bool inWin = minOfDay >= winStartMin
var int  winT  = na
var bool winOk = false
bool winNew = inWin and (na(winT) or winT != dayTs)
if winNew
    winT  := dayTs
    // a window that began on the very first loaded bar may have lost its real start: NA
    winOk := bar_index > 0
bool winUse = inWin and winOk

float body = math.abs(close - open)
float vol  = nz(volume)

var float runLow  = na
var float mbL     = na
var float mvL     = na
var float runHigh = na
var float mbS     = na
var float mvS     = na

if inWin
    // long: a bar whose low <= the running low restarts the window at that bar
    if winNew or low <= runLow
        runLow := low
        mbL    := body
        mvL    := vol
    else
        mbL := math.max(mbL, body)
        mvL := math.max(mvL, vol)
    // short: a bar whose high >= the running high restarts the window at that bar
    if winNew or high >= runHigh
        runHigh := high
        mbS     := body
        mvS     := vol
    else
        mbS := math.max(mbS, body)
        mvS := math.max(mvS, vol)

float bbL = na
float bvL = na
float bbS = na
float bvS = na
if winUse
    bbL := (close > open and body >= mbL) ? 1.0 : 0.0
    bvL := mvL > 0 ? (vol >= mvL ? 1.0 : 0.0) : na
    bbS := (close < open and body >= mbS) ? 1.0 : 0.0
    bvS := mvS > 0 ? (vol >= mvS ? 1.0 : 0.0) : na

// -- The points, both sides ----------------------------------------------------
float h10L = f_ab(close, ema10,  true)
float h1L  = f_ab(close, ema1m,  true)
float h5L  = f_ab(close, ema5,   true)
float h30L = f_ab(close, ema30,  true)
float ylL  = f_ab(close, refYL,  true)
float ycL  = f_ab(close, refYC,  true)
float yhL  = f_ab(close, refYH,  true)

float h10S = f_ab(close, ema10,  false)
float h1S  = f_ab(close, ema1m,  false)
float h5S  = f_ab(close, ema5,   false)
float h30S = f_ab(close, ema30,  false)
float ylS  = f_ab(close, refYL,  false)
float ycS  = f_ab(close, refYC,  false)
float yhS  = f_ab(close, refYH,  false)

// Trend (separate): yesterday's high AND low vs the day before's.
bool trValid = yValid and yyOk and gapYY <= GAP_MAX and not na(yyH) and not na(yyL)
float trL = trValid ? ((yH > yyH and yL > yyL) ? 1.0 : 0.0) : na
float trS = trValid ? ((yH < yyH and yL < yyL) ? 1.0 : 0.0) : na

float totL = nz(h10L) + nz(h1L) + nz(h5L) + nz(h30L) + nz(ylL) + nz(ycL) + nz(yhL) + nz(bbL) + nz(bvL)
float mxL  = f_cnt(h10L) + f_cnt(h1L) + f_cnt(h5L) + f_cnt(h30L) + f_cnt(ylL) + f_cnt(ycL) + f_cnt(yhL) + f_cnt(bbL) + f_cnt(bvL)
float totS = nz(h10S) + nz(h1S) + nz(h5S) + nz(h30S) + nz(ylS) + nz(ycS) + nz(yhS) + nz(bbS) + nz(bvS)
float mxS  = f_cnt(h10S) + f_cnt(h1S) + f_cnt(h5S) + f_cnt(h30S) + f_cnt(ylS) + f_cnt(ycS) + f_cnt(yhS) + f_cnt(bbS) + f_cnt(bvS)

// Which side the labels / alerts follow.
bool  isLongSide = sideIn == "Long" or (sideIn == "Auto" and close >= open)
float autoTot    = isLongSide ? totL : totS
float autoMax    = isLongSide ? mxL : mxS

array<float> curL = array.from(h10L, h1L, h5L, h30L, ylL, ycL, yhL, bbL, bvL, trL, totL, mxL)
array<float> curS = array.from(h10S, h1S, h5S, h30S, ylS, ycS, yhS, bbS, bvS, trS, totS, mxS)
array<float> curR = array.from(ema10, ema1m, ema5, ema30, refYL, refYC, refYH, winUse ? mbL : na, winUse ? mvL : na, winUse ? mbS : na, winUse ? mvS : na, trValid ? yyH : na, trValid ? yyL : na, close)
array<float> curN = array.from(n1, n10tot, n5, n30, trValid ? yH : na, trValid ? yL : na, isLongSide ? 1.0 : 0.0)

// -- Snapshot of the LAST CLOSED bar (the table reads this) --------------------
// Assigned only when the bar is confirmed, so on a live chart the table keeps showing the
// last closed bar while the current bar forms.
var array<float> snapL = array.new_float(12, na)
var array<float> snapS = array.new_float(12, na)
var array<float> snapR = array.new_float(14, na)
var array<float> snapN = array.new_float(7, na)
var int snapT = na
if barstate.isconfirmed
    snapL := curL
    snapS := curS
    snapR := curR
    snapN := curN
    snapT := time

// -- Short names (compact table, labels, tooltips) ----------------------------
var array<string> CMP = array.from("10s", "1m", "5m", "30m", "Y-L", "Y-C", "Y-H", "Body", "Vol")
var array<string> SHORTN = array.from("MA 10s", "MA 1m", "MA 5m", "MA 30m", "Y-L", "Y-C", "Y-H", "Body", "Vol")

f_sc(float tot, float mx) => na(tot) or na(mx) ? "-" : str.tostring(int(tot)) + "/" + str.tostring(int(mx))

// The detail behind a short label: hits, misses, NA and the trend (array = curL / curS layout).
f_tip(array<float> hv, bool isL) =>
    string h = ""
    string m = ""
    string n = ""
    for i = 0 to 8
        float x = array.get(hv, i)
        string nm = array.get(SHORTN, i)
        if na(x)
            n += (n == "" ? "" : ", ") + nm
        else if x > 0.5
            h += (h == "" ? "" : ", ") + nm
        else
            m += (m == "" ? "" : ", ") + nm
    float trv = array.get(hv, 9)
    string trTxt = na(trv) ? "NA" : (trv > 0.5 ? "yes" : "no")
    (isL ? "LONG " : "SHORT ") + f_sc(array.get(hv, 10), array.get(hv, 11)) + " (" + maType + ")\nHit: " + (h == "" ? "none" : h) + "\nMiss: " + (m == "" ? "none" : m) + (n == "" ? "" : "\nNA: " + n) + "\nTrend (not in the score): " + trTxt

// -- Labels --------------------------------------------------------------------
if showLbl and barstate.isconfirmed and autoTot >= labThr
    string lblTxt = f_sc(autoTot, autoMax) + (isLongSide ? " L" : " S")
    string lblTip = f_tip(isLongSide ? curL : curS, isLongSide)
    if isLongSide
        label.new(bar_index, high, lblTxt, style = label.style_label_down, color = color.new(#e6e6e6, 15), textcolor = #101318, size = size.small, tooltip = lblTip)
    else
        label.new(bar_index, low, lblTxt, style = label.style_label_up, color = color.new(#6b7078, 15), textcolor = #ffffff, size = size.small, tooltip = lblTip)

// -- Alerts --------------------------------------------------------------------
// alertcondition: static text, for the classic alert dialog (one per side). Gated with barstate.isconfirmed so it
// can only be true on the CLOSE of a bar (the signal bar S of the spec), never on a still-forming candle, whatever
// frequency the alert dialog is set to.
alertcondition(barstate.isconfirmed and isLongSide and totL >= altThr, title = "Point Score LONG at or above threshold", message = "EDGELOG Point Score: LONG score at or above the alert threshold on {{ticker}} ({{interval}})")
alertcondition(barstate.isconfirmed and not isLongSide and totS >= altThr, title = "Point Score SHORT at or above threshold", message = "EDGELOG Point Score: SHORT score at or above the alert threshold on {{ticker}} ({{interval}})")

// alert(): one message per closed bar with the score and the list of hit points.
if barstate.isconfirmed and autoTot >= altThr
    array<float> autoHv = isLongSide ? curL : curS
    string sideTxt = isLongSide ? "LONG" : "SHORT"
    string alertMsg = '{"symbol":"' + syminfo.tickerid + '","bar_time_ny":"' + str.format_time(time, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm", TZ) + '","side":"' + sideTxt + '","score":"' + str.tostring(int(autoTot)) + "/" + str.tostring(int(autoMax)) + '","hits":[' + f_hits(autoHv) + ']}'
    alert(alertMsg, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// -- Data-window plots: the parity export ---------------------------------------
// display.data_window = not drawn on the chart, present in the Data Window and in
// Export chart data. 1 = hit, 0 = miss, na = not available.
plot(h10L, title = "L ma200_10s", display = display.data_window)
plot(h1L,  title = "L ma200_1m",  display = display.data_window)
plot(h5L,  title = "L ma200_5m",  display = display.data_window)
plot(h30L, title = "L ma200_30m", display = display.data_window)
plot(ylL,  title = "L y_low",     display = display.data_window)
plot(ycL,  title = "L y_close",   display = display.data_window)
plot(yhL,  title = "L y_high",    display = display.data_window)
plot(bbL,  title = "L big_body",  display = display.data_window)
plot(bvL,  title = "L big_vol",   display = display.data_window)
plot(trL,  title = "L trend",     display = display.data_window)
plot(totL, title = "L total",     display = display.data_window)
plot(mxL,  title = "L max",       display = display.data_window)

plot(h10S, title = "S ma200_10s", display = display.data_window)
plot(h1S,  title = "S ma200_1m",  display = display.data_window)
plot(h5S,  title = "S ma200_5m",  display = display.data_window)
plot(h30S, title = "S ma200_30m", display = display.data_window)
plot(ylS,  title = "S y_low",     display = display.data_window)
plot(ycS,  title = "S y_close",   display = display.data_window)
plot(yhS,  title = "S y_high",    display = display.data_window)
plot(bbS,  title = "S big_body",  display = display.data_window)
plot(bvS,  title = "S big_vol",   display = display.data_window)
plot(trS,  title = "S trend",     display = display.data_window)
plot(totS, title = "S total",     display = display.data_window)
plot(mxS,  title = "S max",       display = display.data_window)

plot(ema10, title = "R ema10s", display = display.data_window)
plot(ema1m, title = "R ema1m",  display = display.data_window)
plot(ema5,  title = "R ema5m",  display = display.data_window)
plot(ema30, title = "R ema30m", display = display.data_window)
plot(refYL, title = "R y_low",   display = display.data_window)
plot(refYC, title = "R y_close", display = display.data_window)
plot(refYH, title = "R y_high",  display = display.data_window)

// Extra reference columns for debugging a parity miss (not part of the spec's record).
plot(winUse ? mbL : na, title = "R maxbody_L", display = display.data_window)
plot(winUse ? mvL : na, title = "R maxvol_L",  display = display.data_window)
plot(winUse ? mbS : na, title = "R maxbody_S", display = display.data_window)
plot(winUse ? mvS : na, title = "R maxvol_S",  display = display.data_window)
plot(n1,     title = "R n_1m",  display = display.data_window)
plot(n10tot, title = "R n_10s", display = display.data_window)
plot(n5,     title = "R n_5m",  display = display.data_window)
plot(n30,    title = "R n_30m", display = display.data_window)

// -- Table: the LAST CLOSED bar -------------------------------------------------
var table tb = table.new(f_pos(tblPos), 6, 15, bgcolor = C_BG, border_color = C_BORD, border_width = 1, frame_color = C_BORD, frame_width = 1)
if barstate.islast
    float snapSide = array.get(snapN, 6)
    bool  snapLong = snapSide > 0.5
    array<float> sv = snapLong ? snapL : snapS
    string oneMin = timeframe.period != "1" ? " (1m only!)" : ""
    if layout == "Compact"
        // row 0: MA + the four averages, then the side and the score; row 1: yesterday's levels, body, volume, trend
        table.cell(tb, 0, 0, "MA", text_color = C_DIM, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = C_HDR)
        for k = 0 to 3
            table.cell(tb, 1 + k, 0, array.get(CMP, k), text_color = C_WHITE, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = f_col(array.get(sv, k)))
        table.cell(tb, 5, 0, (snapLong ? "L " : "S ") + f_sc(array.get(sv, 10), array.get(sv, 11)) + oneMin, text_color = C_WHITE, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = C_HDR, tooltip = f_tip(sv, snapLong))
        for k = 4 to 8
            table.cell(tb, k - 4, 1, array.get(CMP, k), text_color = C_WHITE, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = f_col(array.get(sv, k)))
        if showTrend
            table.cell(tb, 5, 1, "trend", text_color = C_WHITE, text_size = size.tiny, bgcolor = f_col(array.get(sv, 9)))
    else if layout == "Minimal"
        float tot = array.get(sv, 10)
        float mx  = array.get(sv, 11)
        color bc  = na(tot) or na(mx) ? C_NA : (tot >= labThr ? C_HIT : (mx > 0 and tot / mx < 0.5 ? C_MISS : C_NA))
        table.cell(tb, 0, 0, f_sc(tot, mx) + (snapLong ? " L" : " S") + oneMin, text_color = C_WHITE, text_size = size.normal, bgcolor = bc, tooltip = f_tip(sv, snapLong))
        if showTrend
            table.cell(tb, 1, 0, "trend", text_color = C_WHITE, text_size = size.tiny, bgcolor = f_col(array.get(sv, 9)))
    else
        // row 0: title, bar time, close
        string hdrTxt = "POINT SCORE  " + (na(snapT) ? "(no closed bar yet)" : str.format_time(snapT, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm", TZ) + " NY") + "   C " + f_px(array.get(snapR, 13))
        table.cell(tb, 0, 0, hdrTxt, text_color = C_TXT, text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = C_HDR)
        table.cell(tb, 1, 0, "", bgcolor = C_HDR)
        table.cell(tb, 2, 0, "", bgcolor = C_HDR)
        table.cell(tb, 3, 0, "", bgcolor = C_HDR)
        table.merge_cells(tb, 0, 0, 3, 0)

        // row 1: warning when the chart is not 1-minute, else which side Auto picked
        string noteTxt = timeframe.period != "1" ? "WARNING: Point Score is defined on 1-minute bars (this chart is " + timeframe.period + ")" : (sideIn == "Auto" ? "Auto side: " + (snapLong ? "LONG (bar closed up)" : "SHORT (bar closed down)") : "Forced side: " + (snapLong ? "LONG" : "SHORT"))
        table.cell(tb, 0, 1, noteTxt, text_color = timeframe.period != "1" ? C_WHITE : C_DIM, text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(tb, 1, 1, "")
        table.cell(tb, 2, 1, "")
        table.cell(tb, 3, 1, "")
        table.merge_cells(tb, 0, 1, 3, 1)

        // row 2: column heads (the followed side is starred)
        table.cell(tb, 0, 2, "Point", text_color = C_DIM, text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = C_HDR)
        table.cell(tb, 1, 2, snapLong ? "Long *" : "Long", text_color = C_DIM, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = snapLong ? C_AUTO : C_HDR)
        table.cell(tb, 2, 2, snapLong ? "Short" : "Short *", text_color = C_DIM, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = snapLong ? C_HDR : C_AUTO)
        table.cell(tb, 3, 2, "Ref", text_color = C_DIM, text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = C_HDR)

        // rows 3-11: the nine points
        for i = 0 to 8
            float hl = array.get(snapL, i)
            float hs = array.get(snapS, i)
            string refTxt = i < 7 ? f_px(array.get(snapR, i)) : (i == 7 ? "L " + f_px(array.get(snapR, 7)) + " | S " + f_px(array.get(snapR, 9)) : "L " + f_int(array.get(snapR, 8)) + " | S " + f_int(array.get(snapR, 10)))
            table.cell(tb, 0, 3 + i, array.get(LBL, i), text_color = C_TXT, text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.small)
            table.cell(tb, 1, 3 + i, f_mark(hl), text_color = f_col(hl), text_size = size.small, bgcolor = snapLong ? C_AUTO : C_BG)
            table.cell(tb, 2, 3 + i, f_mark(hs), text_color = f_col(hs), text_size = size.small, bgcolor = snapLong ? C_BG : C_AUTO)
            table.cell(tb, 3, 3 + i, refTxt, text_color = C_DIM, text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.small)

        // row 12: totals
        table.cell(tb, 0, 12, "Total (of the 9)", text_color = C_TXT, text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = C_HDR)
        table.cell(tb, 1, 12, f_score(array.get(snapL, 10), array.get(snapL, 11)), text_color = C_WHITE, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = snapLong ? C_AUTO : C_HDR)
        table.cell(tb, 2, 12, f_score(array.get(snapS, 10), array.get(snapS, 11)), text_color = C_WHITE, text_size = size.small, bgcolor = snapLong ? C_HDR : C_AUTO)
        table.cell(tb, 3, 12, "", bgcolor = C_HDR)

        // row 13: trend point (separate, never in the /9)
        float trl = array.get(snapL, 9)
        float trs = array.get(snapS, 9)
        string trRef = showTrend and not na(array.get(snapN, 4)) and not na(array.get(snapR, 11)) ? "H " + f_px(array.get(snapN, 4)) + " / " + f_px(array.get(snapR, 11)) + "  L " + f_px(array.get(snapN, 5)) + " / " + f_px(array.get(snapR, 12)) : (showTrend ? "-" : "")
        table.cell(tb, 0, 13, showTrend ? "Daily trend (not in the 9)" : "", text_color = C_DIM, text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(tb, 1, 13, showTrend ? f_mark(trl) : "", text_color = f_col(trl), text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(tb, 2, 13, showTrend ? f_mark(trs) : "", text_color = f_col(trs), text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(tb, 3, 13, trRef, text_color = C_DIM, text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.small)

        // row 14: warm-up counts (an average's point is NA until its timeframe has minBars bars)
        string warmTxt = "Bars loaded: " + f_warm("1m", array.get(snapN, 0)) + " | " + f_warm("10s", array.get(snapN, 1)) + " | " + f_warm("5m", array.get(snapN, 2)) + " | " + f_warm("30m", array.get(snapN, 3))
        table.cell(tb, 0, 14, warmTxt, text_color = C_DIM, text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.small)
        table.cell(tb, 1, 14, "")
        table.cell(tb, 2, 14, "")
        table.cell(tb, 3, 14, "")
        table.merge_cells(tb, 0, 14, 3, 14)
